WEBVTT

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.870
Eiko!

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.410
Takeru, what are you so worked up about?

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:45.980
Teach me English!

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:51.250
<b>Squidn't that English?!</b>

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.220
A foreigner just asked me for directions,

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.580
but I couldn't help him.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.660
So please, teach me English.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.050
Huh? I can't teach you English.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.320
I want to learn English, too.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.850
You don't need it.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.230
I mean, I will be squid-vading 
America at some point, too.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.270
You haven't even gotten 
anywhere with this city,

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.160
but you're already thinking 
about other places?

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.290
Wait a second!

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.430
There's someone perfect 
for teaching English.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:20.820
Coming!

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.130
Whoa, Cindy? 
What's with your clothes?

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:25.850
What, they're normal.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.830
It's not like I'd wear my 
swimsuit to someone's house.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.250
So I guess you do have some common sense.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.410
Where did the glasses come from?

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.300
I usually wear contacts.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.340
Hello.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.310
Hello. You're Takeru, right?

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.670
Yes. Cindy,

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.800
you speak perfect Japanese, 
but you're an American, right?

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.350
Yes, that's right.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:51.980
Man, I wish every 
American was like you.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.220
No squidding way!

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.890
Basics of English Conversation

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.870
All right, let's begin with greetings.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.910
All right!

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.740
Yes!

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.690
Hey, you can speak English after all! 
That's very good!

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.290
I know greetings from watching TV.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:18.660
Hey, what was with that "Teach me English"?

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.220
I didn't even remember any of that!

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.420
I have no inkling what Takeru 
and Cindy are saying!

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.100
You are way more of an Alien than I am!

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.520
This is English, Squid Girlie.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.000
It's fine.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.900
English is like a puzzle,

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.690
so if you grasp the basics, 
it'll be easier than Japanese.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.870
No way...

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:56.550
how could she have learned to 
 speak English in such a short time?

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.800
<i>[nee-chan koori mizu]</i> 
What?! Sister ice water?!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.650
What the hell are you saying?

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.480
Thank you.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.130
Wait...

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.260
"Nature is calling me,"

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.490
which means he has to 
go to the bathroom.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:14.400
What?

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.440
If you need to go to the bathroom, 
you say "Me, toilet, go!" Right?

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.900
Is... that wrong?

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:24.560
But still, your learning 
ability is astonishing.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.260
I'm impressed, Squidian.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.820
I told you that I'm not a Squidian!

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:32.270
It might be more efficient for me to 
focus on teaching the Squidian,

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.000
who can then teach the whole family.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.070
Be taught by Squid Girl!?

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:40.130
You are super stupid.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.880
Like I could endure 
something that humiliating!

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.640
Even my sister...

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.710
I just realized I need to...

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.120
<i>[abunai]</i>
Watch out!

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.290
Huh, what did she say to me?

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.610
Uh...

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.210
Man, I'm thirsty...

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.020
What is this? 
I totally love this stuff.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:38.470
<i>[saikou]</i>
Amazing!

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.320
I should ask where this is from.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:47.340
Oh crap, did I say something weird?

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.640
I should offer her some sweets.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:58.790
I guess she doesn't like this kind of thing.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.620
Just looking at her, she seems like 
she should be a celebrity.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.670
Compared to that, we're just...

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:08.630
<i>[bimbo]</i>
poor.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.280
Meaning: A woman who is attractive but dimwitted.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:15.890
She's mad?

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:19.170
I can't help that we're poor.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.730
Oh, jeez.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.250
<i>[shiran]</i>
I don't care anymore!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:34.360
Huh, she looks kind of sorry now...

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.700
I wonder if she feels bad 
about the "poverty" thing?

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.210
<i> [Mondai nai yo]</i>
Cindy, don't worry about it.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:44.570
Okay, okay. Please, please.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.040
<i>[itadakimasu]</i>
Thanks for the food!

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:58.810
<i>[Udon umai]</i>
The udon noodles are yummy.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.090
Well, I'll have whatever's served to me.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.490
She's eating the eggplant first...

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.080
Maybe she really likes eggplant.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.590
<i>[nasu mittsu]</i>
Three eggplant slices.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.070
Why is Cindy avoiding the wasabi?

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:21.420
She doesn't know what she's missing.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.030
You can eat this.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.550
<i>[arigatou]</i>
Thank you.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:36.520
<i>[o mama goto]</i>
Huh? Playing house?

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.750
Miss Cindy?!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.070
I hope she'll come back...

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.900
It's squidly unlikely.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.080
In the beginning, 
I wasn't so sure about this,

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.700
but in the end we were 
keeping up communication.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:57.660
What's really important isn't the words.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:01.040
Communication is all heart.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.300
Oh, a foreigner.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.690
Squid Girl, you just smile and

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.090
keep quiet, even if he 
asks for directions.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.380
Got it.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.320
Couples go for udon?

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.350
Oh, Yuigahama...

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.680
<i>[aru keru yo]</i>   You can walk there.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.900
See, communication is all heart.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.270
That suits you just fine, Eiko.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.320
Are pictures of dogs really that squidding funny?

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.250
No, it's because you keep tickling me.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.500
What's tickling?

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.930
You're saying you've 
never been tickled?

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:59.910
<b>Ink you can stop it?!</b>

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.530
Squid Girl.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.570
I want you to turn around 
and put out your hands.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.440
Like this?

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.810
And now comes the tickling!

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.380
That's squidding weird!

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.740
That wasn't funny at all, 
but I couldn't stop laughing.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.680
When I do it to myself, 
nothing happens.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:20.910
That's right.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.500
It only works if someone 
else does it to you.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.420
Lemon

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:28.420
Here you go.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.790
Please enjoy.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.960
Obviously, my first victim is...

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:37.660
Please stop!

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.390
I can't stand being tickled!

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:41.720
Oh?

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.770
Hearing that just makes me 
want to tentickle you more!

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.480
Stop acting like a pervy old man!

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.900
You mean you're a pervert now?!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.650
And here's the actual one.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.590
You mean she's not fully grown yet?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.490
I didn't mean it on a 
biological level...

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.660
I taught her about tickling and

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.010
now she wants to try it out on people.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.600
Squid'm!

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.700
What the hell are you doing?!

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.900
Now I get it.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:09.100
You should've just told me earlier.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:12.460
What are you doing?

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:15.710
Squiddie!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.800
Tickle me all you want!

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:21.570
Huh?

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.310
What did you expect?

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:24.670
Take this!

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:25.910
Take that!

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:26.910
Koochie koochie coo!

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.720
And this! And that!

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.080
Damn it!

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.520
She's taking this too far!

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.890
What the hell are you 
doing to the customers?!

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:38.240
I'm sorry, I got a squiddle carried away.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:42.930
But maybe I stand a chance 
against Chizuru with this.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.590
I really wouldn't go after 
my sister if I were you.

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:46.940
But why?

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:49.790
Because getting tickled is about 
the only thing she can't stand.

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.210
Oh, I think that's perfect.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.140
Don't you get it?

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:57.880
Tickling my sister who hates 
to be tickled is tantamount to

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.930
an all-out declaration of war.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:03.100
Sure, but come on...

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.760
Don't you want to see

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.820
Chizuru rolling on the floor laughing?

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.230
I do...

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:10.460
It'll be fine.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:14.290
She wouldn't get mad just 
because I made her laugh a squiddle.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.400
It would be more like a 
form of communication.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.390
Here I go.

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:20.040
Take care.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.870
She's so scared that she had 
to use auto-suggestion...

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:28.580
And now!

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.210
Looks like you let your 
guard down, Chizuru.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.040
It's death by laughter!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:42.090
I'm sorry, Squid Girl, 
but I'm not ticklish there.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:43.950
But...

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:47.380
Then where the squid do I tickle 
you to make you lose it?

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:50.230
I'm afraid I can't tell you that.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:55.480
But I will acknowledge 
your declaration of war.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:08.600
So I guess this is what death 
by laughter feels like.

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.450
You were brave.

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.650
That was a sheer joy to watch!

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:15.430
Thank you, Squiddie!

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:16.960
What?

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.070
Hiccups?

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.100
They're probably from 
laughing too much.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:26.480
Did you know that if you 
can't stop by the 100th hiccup,

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.700
something horrible will happen to you?

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.520
One hundred?
 I don't have that much squidding time.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:33.070
For squid people,

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:35.760
something horrible happens 
to you after thirty hiccups.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:36.700
Huh?

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:41.270
You can't just apply human 
standards to squids like me.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:43.520
So do you have some kind of remedy?

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.030
Of course!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.300
I have to be made happy!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.430
I'm going on break.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:55.580
It's true! I can't help it!

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.960
Look, I only have 26 hiccups left!

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.950
Talk about a pain...

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:03.420
Then tell us: 
what would make you happy?

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:06.810
If I told you, 
it would have no meaning!

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.800
You have to try to anticipate what

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.120
would make me happy 
and make it a surprise!

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:13.390
You are a serious pain.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:17.380
What if I let you win at video games?

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:19.990
A massage fit for a celebrity?

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.070
An allowance?

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:24.710
Hey!

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:26.600
Here...

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.310
Be satisfied, already!

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.610
What you're doing isn't enough!

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:36.060
We're trying to cooperate with you,

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.210
so why are you being so difficult?

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:39.820
And are you really going to die

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:42.390
once you hit thirty hiccups?

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:45.670
I never said I would die.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:46.380
Huh?

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:49.340
However, my tentacles will 
mutate in this grotesque way

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:52.040
and start attacking anybody and everybody.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.140
Are you serious?

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:58.690
I don't want to keep doing this 
and have you end up spoiled...

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:00.520
Sis?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.930
Well, Squiddie?

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:04.900
It's an exquisite meal 
featuring the Spiny Lobster!

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.990
It looks lovely!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.220
I'm so full.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:12.810
So, how are you now?

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:14.800
Hmm... let's see.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:18.330
Huh?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.370
I've had enough of this.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.570
What the squid are you doing?

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.770
Threatening me won't make 
the hiccups go away!

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.430
Looks like she's really serious.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:34.120
We've indulged your 
little whims until now,

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.980
but it stops right here.

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.900
Any last words?

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.420
I'm sorry for everything I squidding did!

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:45.070
I'm sorry for tickling you, too!

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:48.820
Farewell then, Squid Girl...

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.280
No!!!

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.500
Just kidding!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.800
Sorry.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.940
That was a little act 
to stop the hiccups!

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:08.590
I thought you were going to krill me.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:12.010
I'm alive! I'm alive, aren't I?

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.160
Oh?

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.970
It looks like the hiccups stopped.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.350
They did!

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:18.560
I'm so glad!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.400
It's so good to be squidding alive!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.250
I'm glad the hiccups stopped.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:27.560
There really isn't a better 
surprise than that.

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:30.610
This is the highest form of happiness!

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:36.620
Eiko, I'm going to play by 
the river with my friends!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:37.610
All right.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.950
Take care though!

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.670
I'm going, too!

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:42.620
Hey!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.380
You've got work to do.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.590
Sometimes, I want to 
get some time off, too!

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.090
"Sometimes," she says...

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.880
Well, I guess it's okay if 
you're going to watch out for

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:58.810
Takeru and his friends so they
don't get washed away.

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:01.000
I will!

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:06.550
<b>Get my drift?!</b>

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.560
It's like a long, narrow ocean.

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:16.830
It's called a river, Squid Girlie.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.550
You got her to come along.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.460
Good job, Takeru!

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.790
Uh, yeah.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.260
What are you going to do?

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.090
There's no sand like by the Lemon,

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:31.030
so we can't make a castle.

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:32.760
Beach volleyball would 
be dangerous, too.

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:34.020
I've got an idea.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.600
Let's race bamboo boats!

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.020
Yeah!

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.020
Bamboo boats?

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.520
Do you know how to make a bamboo boat?

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:43.280
I have no squidding idea.

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:46.480
Bend both of those sides over.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:47.480
Okay...

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:51.570
You make cuts that divide it 
into about three sections.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.870
I see...

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:56.500
Leave out the middle and stick 
it in the end like this...

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:57.320
Uh huh...

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.530
And you're done!

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:01.410
Takeru, that's exsquidsite!

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.830
You turned a single leaf into a boat!

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:05.670
I'm seeing you in a whole new light!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:09.240
It's not that impressive.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:14.130
Bend here... three sections.... 
stick it in here and here...

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:16.120
Squidtastic!

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:19.600
I'm going to call this 
ship "Black Tiger"!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:22.310
What's with the stone inside?

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:26.200
What is that stone supposed to do?

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:28.770
Why, it's me, of course!

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.740
A boat with nobody in it can 
hardly be called a boat!

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:38.770
Everyone, hurry up and 
let's start the race!

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:43.240
Shouldn't we tell her?

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.700
That boat is totally going to sink.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:48.720
Yeah, but she's got her pride.

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:49.840
Yeah, huh?

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.320
Why don't you all just cool down.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:53.260
What?

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.200
Do you have some kind of idea?

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:59.050
I anticipated this, which is why 
I brought this pumice stone.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.070
Wow, that's awesome!

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:02.560
It really is.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.560
Squid Girlie?

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.730
About that rock in your bamboo bo- 
I mean, in your "Black Tiger."

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.980
I was thinking this white rock

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:12.940
suits you a lot better than that one... 
What do you say?

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:13.760
Yeah!

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.420
Then why don't I use that?

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.780
Aren't you guys going to get ready?

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:21.240
It's still floating!

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.230
Good!

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.290
I guess it won't sink now.

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:25.690
Listen up.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:28.420
She's a very bad loser,

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:31.750
and if she doesn't come out on top, 
she gets really mad...

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:35.710
There's no squidding way my 
Black Tiger could lose!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.090
She'd hate us all!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:38.930
Yeah...

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:41.520
Their impression of her is...

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:45.050
We have to let her win, no matter what!

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:46.100
Yeah!

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:47.980
Then let's start!

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:52.360
Oh no!

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:54.860
Attack!

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.040
Kaboom!

00:18:58.520 --> 00:18:59.960
Laser attack!

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.480
Giant on the loose!

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:11.250
Squid Girlie's Black Tiger really is awesome!

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.950
That boat is unbeatable!

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.480
It's awesome!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:17.760
Squid Girlie, where are you going?

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:21.320
I'm sitting in the Black Tiger GT,

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.720
so I've got to see how far she goes!

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.180
Squid Girlie...

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:33.900
This is amazing. 
It just keeps going and going.

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.650
Squiiii!!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.740
Squii, squii!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.760
Squii, squii!

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.990
My Black Tiger Ticonderoga

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:15.000
went back to the sea.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:17.200
The sea?

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:20.150
This is the sea.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:26.440
The river and the sea are connected.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:30.120
I guess that means that 
all things on the surface

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.560
go back to the sea.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:35.290
Oh, it's the Lemon.

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:40.730
I guess that means this is 
where this squid finds her "home."

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:45.450
I'm back!

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:47.030
Welcome.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.330
To the house on the beach, Lenon!

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:54.300
Lenon

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:52.600
Le-Lenon?

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:59.960
Where the squid am I?!

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:04.890
Squid Girlie isn't coming back, huh?

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:05.880
Yeah.

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:08.650
How far did that fool go?

00:23:40.990 --> 00:23:43.400
Squiddie, I love you. I adore you!

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:44.900
This is Sanae Nagatsuki.

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:45.690
The next three episodes will be:

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:47.170
I ink that's radio-controlled?!

00:23:47.170 --> 00:23:48.710
Squidn't it Tanabata?!

00:23:48.710 --> 00:23:50.340
A squiddle playtime alone?!

00:23:50.340 --> 00:23:52.060
Please watch how the love between

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:53.640
Squiddie and myself blossoms.
